Correction recorded rather than quietly dropped. When recommending that
role=slider move onto the container, I cited unreliable SVG tabindex focus in
WebKit as a reason. The probe added here finds <g tabindex="0"> focusable in
Chromium, WebKit and Firefox alike, so the claim did not hold for the engines
this project actually targets.

The design decision is unchanged, because the reasons that survive are
sufficient on their own - fewer adapters altered, natural ownership of the
describedby/keyshortcuts/live-region wiring, and the focus-visibility fix that
moving off the handle enabled. But the stated rationale was wrong and is
corrected in the vue and svelte spec deltas, index.md, and the Vue test header.

The probe is kept as a committed spec that reports rather than enforces, so
this stays verifiable instead of reverting to folklore.
